in{aligned}-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n2+(-3)+(-2)=-3.\n$$" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281202 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1069 "q-163086" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1071 "![](images/32/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1072 #uuid "58c426d1-6e48-58eb-96d9-a5133f5b4952" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281598 1074 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281015 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1069 "q-163087" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1071 "![](images/32/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1072 #uuid "930d6994-09ee-58f8-aa72-d60045e82fbb" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281599 1074 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $\\frac{34}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280918 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1069 "q-163088" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1071 "For the function of two variables \n$f(x,y)={e}^{xy},$\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=a+bxy.\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b.$" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1072 #uuid "40019177-315b-5f8c-afeb-29b9f1c22ad3" 13194139533405 17592186045585 true] [17592186281600 1074 "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at $(x,y)=(0,0),$ then the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈\\overset{\\text{Linear approximation}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(0,0)+{f}_{x}(0,0)\\cdot x+{f}_{y}(0,0)\\cdot y}} \\\\  & \\,\\,+{{\\frac{1}{2}({f}_{xx}(0,0)\\cdot {x}^{2}+2{f}_{xy}(0,0)\\cdot xy+{f}_{yy}(0,0)\\cdot {